# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF regardless of what an
# individual agent's editor wrote on checkout (this tree is written to by
# agents on Windows, producing a mix of LF and CRLF). Git stores LF and
# converts to the platform's native line ending on checkout only if the
# platform needs it — Windows tools that require CRLF should set
# core.autocrlf locally, not rely on repo content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch/PowerShell scripts genuinely need CRLF to run correctly
# outside WSL/git-bash — keep those native.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary types some future asset drop may add — never touched by EOL
# normalization even if extensionless detection guesses wrong.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
